# The programme catalogue lives here: one file per programme, named after its
# slug, holding a title, a slug, an optional family identifier and an optional
# description. The slug is the canonical identifier a course or an assignment
# refers to. The family is an id from the programme_families list in
# data/vocab/associates.yml, never the family wording written out again.
#
# Each record names exactly one family. A programme that spans two is two
# programmes; a `family` given as a list fails the build.
#
# A programme does not list its courses. Each course names one programme in its
# own front matter, and the programme page collects those courses, so a course
# cannot end up under two programmes.
#
# A README.md cannot live in this folder: Hugo loads everything under data/ as
# site data and fails on a file it cannot unmarshal. The catalogue is documented
# in README.md at the repository root, under "Programme catalogue".
